  "worked_solution": "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2{x}^{5/2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\cdot {2}^{5/2}-2\\cdot {0}^{5/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{{c}^{3}} & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
